Premiere:
November 20th 2025, Studio 6, Amare, Den Haag
Scoring:
Alto Flute, Bass Clarinet in Bb, Trumpet in C, Violin, Violoncello, Contrabass 
Program note: Chain of Thoughts is a generative composition, created as part of the doctoral research Performative
Transactions: Worlding Compositional Ecosystems. The work is based on a score of interdependent
textual prompts that guide an AI agent to compose one bar at a time within a blockchain-based
compositional environment known as the Decentralised Creative Network (DCN). Each prompt
specifies operational instructions—such as relationships between instruments, texture, register, or
dynamics—without prescribing exact notes. The reasoning AI agent (GPT-5) interprets every
instruction in the context of everything generated so far, continually querying and expanding the
DCN as it composes (it takes around 1 hour of reasoning or 1 million tokens to generate one part of
the piece). This process produces a unique score on every execution while preserving the provenance
of its underlying compositional logic. In principle, the score exists as a chain of prompts for the AI
model to interpret. Thus, Chain of Thoughts can generate an infinite number of versions, each an
individuation of the same chain of compositional operations. For this concert, however, three parts in
three versions were curated from the pool of generated material, and are intended to be presented in
one continuous performance. The order planned for the premiere is:
1) Part 1 Version 1—Pages 1-8,
2) Part 2 Version 1—Pages 9-13,
3) Part 3 Version 1—Pages 14-17,
4) Part 1 Version 2—Pages 18-26,
5) Part 3 Version 2—Pages 27-30,
6) Part 2 Version 2—Pages 31-35,
7) Part 3 Version 3—Pages 36-39,
8) Part 2 Version 3—Pages 40-44,
9) Part 1 Version 3—Pages 45-52.
Together ca. 12 minutes.
By presenting these three versions consecutively, the concert reveals the generative space defined by
the work: instead of a fixed musical text, Chain of Thoughts is a system of reasoning and variation,
where the performers, the AI agent, and the composer together explore the evolving potential of the
same compositional structure.
More versions of this piece can be generated by following instructions with this dedicated software:
https://github.com/sunsetsobserver/chain-of-thoughts/
The detailed text prompts used to generate this music score can be explored at:
